Contract: `Snapshot` returns an independent point-in-time copy of the cache that callers may read or mutate without coordinating with the cache's lock. The cache is updated by background goroutines through `Set`. The code is:

```go
type Cache struct {
    mu    sync.RWMutex
    items map[string]int
}

func (c *Cache) Set(k string, v int) {
    c.mu.Lock()
    defer c.mu.Unlock()
    c.items[k] = v
}

func (c *Cache) Snapshot() map[string]int {
    c.mu.RLock()
    defer c.mu.RUnlock()
    return c.items
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
